'''Baccara''' ({{Literal translation|black rose}}) is a [[Planned communities in Balisca|planned community]] in the [[Arapytúcaá]] region of the [[Araucaria|Araucarian community]]. Developed in the 1990s to encourage affordable housing and urban decentralization in central Araucaria, it began to perform its own administrative and cultural functions in 2011, as the population density gradually increased. 

Under the ambitious goals of the [[Casajuan Plan]], it aims to accommodate more than additional 31,000 households by 2030, the majority of which are projected to be [[Immigration to Balisca|incoming migrants]] to Balisca. 

